From f0726ceede68cf3269010704863c1cc0c96ce6dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:58:32 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(post): lathe posts reset surface speed at each
 section's end

A section's SurfaceSpeed PARAM set sCss and nothing reset it, so a
later section that stated none still posted G96 with the machine-max
cap instead of its own G97 S<rpm> - a drill on centre would run at the
spindle maximum. Both lathe posts (Fanuc, PathPilot) now clear sCss in
endPreamble(), beside the other per-section asks. Pinned by a
two-section stream (CSS turning, then an axial drill with no CSS) in
each post's suite.

Fixes #772

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
